.TH KINTSUGI-INIT 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-init \- scaffold a workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi init
[\-\-force]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draft CONTEXT.md and kintsugi.toml from the current directory tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing files
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize a workspace:
.PP
  $ kintsugi init
.PP
Force reinitialize:
.PP
  $ kintsugi init --force
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-context (1)
